                    briefing_text_r3:       `Zero of 312 courses carry a business-impact measure, and the CEO already rejected completion and satisfaction as proof. For three flagship programs, choose what to measure across the Kirkpatrick/business-outcome logic: behavior change, leading operational indicators (service-contract <strong>attach rate</strong>, <strong>mean-time-to-resolution</strong>), and a <strong>business-impact index</strong> linking learning to a 2030 commercial metric. Define baselines, owners and data sources, and <em>name the weakest link in the causal chain honestly</em> — and decide where measurement is worth its cost.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Pitch to the Board and govern the trade-off`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present the redesign to the CEO/CFO against the <strong>30%-cut alternative</strong> (EUR 4.4M, two academies, 11 of 40 roles). Show the before/after on all four KPIs, name what you gave up to fund the capability shift, and defend it <em>inside the freeze — asking for more money is what triggered the audit</em>. Then commit to a governance cadence: without quarterly realignment checkpoints, your alignment score decays back to 34% by inertia. The facilitator will stress-test one assumption live — concede the weakest link and lead with evidence, or watch the function fold into shared services.`,

                    r1_diag_label:          `How do you classify the EUR 14.6M of spend against the five 2030 priorities?`,
