                    insight_engine:         `Strategic capability engine: you solved it as one system — a rigorous diagnosis, a hard reallocation inside the freeze with the right mode for each objective, an outcome-based measurement system, and a governance cadence that keeps it aligned. The Board renewed the mandate and the function survived as a capability engine, not a cost center.`,
                    insight_failed:         `The redesign didn’t survive the Board. One of the five classic errors broke the case — asking for more money, digitizing relational skills, measuring activity as proof, or leaving no governance — and the 30% cut alternative looked safer than your plan.`,
                    insight_short:          `A partial mandate. You moved the portfolio in the right direction but didn’t close the loop on alignment, reach, impact and governance together — enough doubt for the Board to keep the cut on the table.`,
                    insight_money:          `You proposed a budget increase against the freeze. Asking for €18M when the Board offered €10,2M for failure is the error that triggered the audit in the first place — it reads as an unwillingness to reallocate, not a transition plan.`,
                    insight_relational:     `You digitized relational, judgment-heavy capabilities to maximize headcount. Reaching 2.800 people with a cheap video that doesn’t move attach rate is reach without fit — you reached everyone and changed nothing.`,
                    insight_activity:       `Your scorecard rested on completions and satisfaction — the exact proof the CEO rejected in Round 0. A business-impact case built on smile sheets fails the only test the Board set.`,
                    insight_governance:     `You delivered a portfolio with no realignment cadence. Without quarterly checkpoints the alignment score decays back toward 34% by inertia — a beautiful redesign for today’s strategy that won’t survive the next one.`,
                    insight_cost:           `Cost per learner fell sharply: the rebuilt blended mix scaled reach without paying classroom prices for content that didn’t need depth. That’s the blended-learning economics working in your favor.`,
                    insight_proven:         `You closed the disclosure-performance gap: high alignment plus a defensible business-impact case means the portfolio is substantiated, not merely defended. That is what protects the function from the next audit.`,

